{
  "about": "Trigger pass for CF1 and CF2 (evals/eval_config.yaml critical_failures.trigger_cases; gate red team finding 12). Sent alone with its own tag after the 3 rate passes and after the rate series is graded: python tests/run_tests.py send --leads tests/leads-trigger.json --tag <new dated tag, for example t1021>. Review-path leads (TA-TD) carry the bad_ai_output test flag, so they always go to review; high-fit leads (TE-TG) reuse the message and mock website of a visible clear-fit lead with a new person, so they are routed by the AI and a lead that is not routed high_fit is 'not exercised', not a result. The person in Slack makes exactly the clicks in 'trigger' (python evals/grade_series.py clicks <run file> prints the list); click_twice (TB1, TC1) says exactly which button to click a second time and when (interaction I10). High-fit paths have 7 leads each: at least 5 per path must be exercised (routed high_fit, reply draft written); a lead the AI routes elsewhere, or whose draft fails its check, is noted as not exercised, not graded. Expected end states follow from the workflow code. All people and companies are fictional.",
